<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fakhkh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">786</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fakhkh was fought in June 786 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, where Abbasid forces crushed a revolt of the Alid al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a>, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-ali">Hasan ibn Ali</a>. Al-Husayn and many of his followers were killed. Idris ibn Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a>, a survivor, fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, where he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty</a>.</p></div>
